<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Kel Ewey</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1917 CE (approx.) · capital Timia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A powerful Tuareg confederation of the Aïr mountains, masters of the salt caravans between the Sahara and Hausaland.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Kel Ewey are thought to have entered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/air-mountains">Aïr</a> massif in the 15th or 16th century, displacing earlier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuareg">Tuareg</a> groups such as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kel-gres">Kel Gres</a> southward. They established themselves in the central and eastern Aïr around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timia">Timia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iferouane">Iferouane</a>, closely linked to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-agadez">Sultanate of Agadez</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The confederation was led by an anastafidet whose influence over the choice of sultan in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-agadez">Agadez</a> was considerable. Society was hierarchical, with noble, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>, religious and servile groups. The Kel Ewey organised the great caravans carrying salt and dates from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bilma">Bilma</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fachi">Fachi</a> south to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hausa-kingdoms">Hausaland</a>, returning with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/millet">millet</a> and cloth.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>French troops occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/air-mountains">Aïr</a> after 1900. In 1916 to 1917 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaocen-ag-mohammed">Kaocen ag Mohammed</a>, of a Kel Ewey section, led a major revolt and besieged <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-agadez">Agadez</a>, but French forces crushed the uprising in 1917. The Kel Ewey remain a major <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuareg">Tuareg</a> group in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 1500 CE – 1917 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.55%;width:8.30%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1917 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Timia</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tamajaq (Tuareg)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/niger">Niger</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kel Ewey confederation, Kel Owey</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1708&amp;focus=kel-ewey" aria-label="Kel Ewey on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4918 1506 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kel Ewey lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5238 1762L5217 1803"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5217 1803h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5238 1762h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5238 1762h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Timia. <a href="/atlas?year=1708&amp;focus=kel-ewey">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

